content.text:
instructure-design-tokens now have the possibility of carrying a 'modify' set, which currently consists of 'alpha', 'darken', and 'lighten' which look like:
lighten:
```
        "mobileNav": {
          "value": "{color.grey.grey10}",
          "type": "color",
          "$extensions": {
            "studio.tokens": {
              "modify": {
                "type": "lighten",
                "value": "0.5",
                "space": "hsl"
              }
            }
          }
        },
```
darken:
```
    "arrowsBackgroundHoverColor": {
      "value": "{semantic.color.institutional.brandButtonSecondaryBgd}",
      "type": "color",
      "$extensions": {
        "studio.tokens": {
          "modify": {
            "type": "darken",
            "value": "0.1",
            "space": "hsl"
          }
        }
      }
    },
```
alpha:
```
        "brandButtonSecondaryBgd": {
          "value": "{color.navy.navy60}",
          "type": "color",
          "$extensions": {
            "studio.tokens": {
              "modify": {
                "type": "alpha",
                "value": "0.3",
                "space": "hsl"
              }
            }
          }
        },
```
we should deterministically resolve the computed value in our flattened IR so that the tokens we provide are simply the appropriate color and this carries into the css properties, etc.  we should validate every component of these extensions/modifiers.  Is the modifier a valid type? (alpha, lighten, darken) is the value a valid increment (0.00 -> 1.00), is the upstream token/token reference a color?  If it also carries a modifier, how do we resolve it?
broken modifiers should be collected in known-syntax-issues.json so they can be manually resolved and blessed.

